From 6171e191b2da9b60a9a944cd6c618022d1491345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "SN Fast Sync (local)" <snfast@localhost.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:09:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] fix(services): reconnect the websocket with back-off,
 and catch up after it was down

WebSocketsService reconnected at once, with no back-off, when the socket closed (a refused connection made it loop at
network speed), and if the token request failed during a reconnect the failure was dropped silently: nothing scheduled
another attempt, so the push channel stayed dead until the app was restarted (SyncService then fell back to the 30 s
timer). Now a failed token request or connection schedules a retry (immediate, then 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 30 s, repeating the
last delay), a second start while a socket is open or connecting is ignored, a close event of an already replaced socket
is ignored, and closing the connection cancels pending retries. Notifications sent while the socket was down are lost, so
the service emits a new ConnectionReestablished event on a reconnect and SyncService answers it with one catch-up sync.
New restartWebSocketConnection() replaces a socket that may be silently dead (used when a phone app returns to the front).
Two starts can no longer run at the same time (isStartingConnection). Unit tests (jest, fake timers and a fake WebSocket) cover the
retry after a failed token request, the back-off, the catch-up event and the restart; three of them fail on the previous code.
